{"name":"Strike a Pose","hex":"#5a4659","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"strike","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To delete or cross out; to scratch or eliminate.","To have a sharp or sudden physical effect, as of a blow."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A status resulting from a batter swinging and missing a pitch, or not swinging at a pitch when the ball goes in the strike zone, or hitting a foul ball that is not caught.","The act of knocking down all ten pins on the first roll of a frame."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strike"},{"term":"pose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Common cold, head cold; catarrh."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To place in an attitude or fixed position, for the sake of effect.","To ask; to set (a test, quiz, riddle, etc.)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vogue (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Vogue\" is a song by American singer Madonna from her soundtrack album I'm Breathless (1990). Written and produced by herself and Shep Pettibone, it was inspired by voguing, a dance popularized in New York City in the late 1980s. The song was released as the lead single from the album on March 20, 1990, by Sire Records and Warner Bros. Records. \"Vogue\" is a house song with influences of disco; it contains escapist lyrics describing the dance floor as \"a place where no boundaries exist\". Its middle eight features Madonna name-dropping several actors from the Golden Age of Hollywood. \"Vogue\" was later included on three of Madonna's compilation albums: The Immaculate Collection (1990), Celebration (2009), and Finally Enough Love: 50 Number Ones (2022)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/81/Madonna%2C_Vogue_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vogue_(song)"},{"title":"Strike a Pose","blocks":[{"text":"Strike a Pose is a Belgian-Dutch documentary film, which premiered in the Panorama section of the 2016 Berlinale. Directed by Ester Gould and Reijer Zwaan, the film profiles the dancers who performed with Madonna on her Blond Ambition World Tour in 1990."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4d/Strike_a_Pose_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strike_a_Pose"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/81/Madonna%2C_Vogue_cover.png/250px-Madonna%2C_Vogue_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/81/Madonna%2C_Vogue_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/81/Madonna%2C_Vogue_cover.png/250px-Madonna%2C_Vogue_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMadonna%2C_Vogue_cover.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/David_Fincher_%282012%29_3.jpg/250px-David_Fincher_%282012%29_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/67/David_Fincher_%282012%29_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/David_Fincher_%282012%29_3.jpg/250px-David_Fincher_%282012%29_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"David Fincher, who had previously directed two of Madonna's music videos, was appointed as the director for \"Vogue\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADavid_Fincher_(2012)_3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9c/Voguem.jpeg/250px-Voguem.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=p